      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $M$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $M?$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $M$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
